          "evidence_id": "evidence-ed7e35043048",
          "exact": "A Red-Black Tree is a self-balancing binary search tree with a height limit of O(logN), enabling efficient search, insertion, and deletion operations in O(logN) time, unlike standard binary search trees which can take O(N) time.\n- Each node has an additional attribute: a color, which can be either red or black.\n- These colors are used to maintain balance during insertions and deletions, ensuring efficient data retrieval and manipulation."
